review_comments.body:
Good catch. I've pushed a fix for this, along with a rebase against latest trunk. The fix is simply to add:
```java
if (stateMgr.approximateNumUncommittedBytes() > 0) {
    commitNeeded = true;
}
```
to `StreamTask`, immediately after `initializeTopology();`. This ensures that, in the event that initializing the topology and its processors writes data to the transaction buffers, a commit is immediately requested. Since `approximateNumUncommittedBytes() > 0` requires data to be in the transaction buffers, this implicitly requires transactional state stores to be enabled to have any effect.

